# GMS never prints the afterimage's rate. Every language says only "fires at set
# intervals", and the client doesn't hold it either: neither 400031020 nor
# 400031021 has a `summon` node, which marks a pulse timed by the server (see
# periodic_intervals). So the rate is the user's own observation, one attack a
# second. `subTime 180` is not the rate; reading it that way once made the
# afterimage fire five times too fast.
#
# GMS gives the buff 30 seconds and the afterimages 3, adding 3 more for each
# second their attacks land, up to the buff's length. A Bow Master never stops
# attacking, so the afterimages simply fire for the whole 30.
#
# One enemy per volley. GMS states no mobCount, and though the hitbox fits 24 by
# the reach rule, that rule only lowers a stated cap, it doesn't create one.
#
# The passive counts ten of the character's own attacks. Hurricane's
# hits_per_attack_count defines an attack, so the rate follows Hurricane if it
# ever changes. Its afterimage lasts `q` = 1 second and strikes once a second,
# so it gets one attack of 3 lines. GMS states a lifetime and an attackCount but
# never a repeat count.
name: "Inhuman Speed"
description:
  "Causes you to attack so quickly you produce afterimages. Unaffected by "
  "attack reflection. After performing a certain number of attacks while the "
  "active effect of the skill isn't active, an afterimage is created that "
  "attacks for a short time."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
buff {
  duration_seconds: 30.0
  pulse {
    label: "Afterimage"
    cast_interval_seconds: 1.0
    max_enemies: 1
    lines: 3
    base { skill_pct: 4.16 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.16 }
  }
}
auto_mode {
  label: "Passive Afterimage"
  attacks_per_cast: 10
  max_enemies: 1
  lines: 3
  silent_while_buff_stands: true
  base { skill_pct: 4.16 }
  per_level { skill_pct: 0.16 }
}
